  <Docs>
    <summary>Encapsulates the information needed to display a notification as a bubble.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>Encapsulates the information needed to display a notification as a bubble. A bubble is used to display app content in a floating window over the existing foreground activity. A bubble has a collapsed state represented by an icon and an expanded state that displays an activity. These may be defined via Builder.Builder(PendingIntent,Icon) or they may be defined via an existing shortcut using Builder.Builder(String).</para>
      <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/app/Notification.BubbleMetadata" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.app.Notification.BubbleMetadata</code>.</a></format></para>
